* INA241A2 - BEHAVIORAL model written for the OPEN_PHASE project
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* This is NOT a Texas Instruments model (TI does not provide an LTspice model).
* It reproduces the documented behaviour of the INA241A2 (SBOSA30D) closely
* enough to study the signal chain between the shunt and the ADC:
*   - VOUT = (VREF1 + VREF2)/2 + 20 x (VIN+ - VIN-)      (datasheet equation 1)
*   - -3 dB bandwidth 1.1 MHz (single pole), slew rate 8 V/us
*   - output swing GND + 8 mV ... VS - 70 mV (typical, RL = 10 k)
*   - quiescent current 2.5 mA, input bias current 35 uA per input
* Not modelled: noise, CMRR and the 1 us output hold of the enhanced PWM
* rejection (the output of this model does not react at all to the common-mode
* voltage). Gain and input offset are the parameters G and Vos: nominal by
* default, drawn inside the datasheet limits by the Monte Carlo simulation 08.
* Parameters not given in the datasheet (REF pin network 2 x 50 k, closed-loop
* output resistance 0.5 ohm) are engineering estimates.
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Pins: IN+ IN- REF1 REF2 VS GND OUT
.subckt INA241A2_BEHAV INP INN REF1 REF2 VS COM OUT
.param G=20 Vos=0 fbw=1.1Meg SR=8Meg Cp=1n
* --- supply and input bias currents -----------------------------------------
Iq VS COM 2.5m
Ibp INP COM 35u
Ibn INN COM 35u
* --- reference network: output is centred on the mid-point of REF1 / REF2 ----
Rr1 REF1 mid 50k
Rr2 REF2 mid 50k
* --- gain, clamped to the output swing --------------------------------------
Bt tgt COM V=min(max(V(mid,COM)+G*(V(INP,INN)+Vos), 8m), V(VS,COM)-70m)
* --- 1.1 MHz pole with 8 V/us slew limit (gm = 2*pi*fbw*Cp, Imax = SR*Cp) ----
Bs COM pole I=limit(2*pi*fbw*Cp*V(tgt,pole), -SR*Cp, SR*Cp)
Cp pole COM {Cp}
Rp pole COM 1G
* --- output buffer ------------------------------------------------------------
Eo buf COM pole COM 1
Ro buf OUT 0.5
.ends INA241A2_BEHAV
